  <mdb:resourceLineage>
    <mrl:LI_Lineage>
      <mrl:statement>
        <gco:CharacterString>Canonical H3 resolution-11 cells classified as nonmarine are dissolved by shared edges and polygon union without coarsening. The marine classification combines permanent-water status with cell-centre intersections against Overture ocean polygons. The footprint includes islands and inland water. Processing uses a precision grid of 1e-10 degrees. Source coordinates are retained without smoothing; project UUIDs identify the dissolved geometry objects. This polygon footprint is not a DEM elevation contour or a surveyed shoreline. Public schema omits repeated validity diagnostics and internal processing fields. Original evidence remains in the workflow audit; public IDs, geometry and retained attributes are unchanged. Source processing summary: {"nonmarine_cells": 61088885, "h3_resolution": 11, "polygon_parts": 1836, "interior_rings": 172}.</gco:CharacterString>
      </mrl:statement>
      <mrl:source>
        <mrl:LI_Source>
          <mrl:description>
            <gco:CharacterString>Project H3 R11 nonmarine classification</gco:CharacterString>
          </mrl:description>
        </mrl:LI_Source>
      </mrl:source>
    </mrl:LI_Lineage>
